aims-os-welcome (2.1+2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * runtimes.sh: verify every Bun / Deno / uv download against the
    sha256 each project publishes in the same release (SHASUMS256.txt,
    .sha256sum, .sha256). Catches corrupted or truncated downloads
    before the binaries land in /usr/local/bin.
  * rstudio.sh: amd64 now pulls the stable channel
    (download1.rstudio.org, 2026.07.1-147) with the sha256 from
    Posit's downloads manifest. arm64 stays on the pinned dailies
    build (the only arm64 .deb source) with its bytes pinned by
    sha256. Both installs refuse to proceed on a hash mismatch.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:40:00 +0000

aims-os-welcome (2.1+1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ship the six post-install scripts under /usr/share/aims-os/install/.
    Each one mirrors one of the v2.0 chroot hooks that we disabled to
    slim the ISO; they're now idempotent and safe to run on an
    installed system:
      nodejs.sh     NodeSource Node 22 LTS
      vscodium.sh   VSCodium via paulcarroty apt repo
      cursor.sh     Cursor .deb from cursor.com
      dbeaver.sh    DBeaver CE via upstream apt repo
      runtimes.sh   Bun + Deno + uv from GitHub releases
      rstudio.sh    RStudio Desktop .deb from Posit
  * Add Depends: curl, gnupg, ca-certificates, unzip — the runtime
    deps these scripts need. The wizard (step 4) will drive them via
    pkexec; users can run them by hand in the meantime.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Wed, 03 Jun 2026 11:30:00 +0000

aims-os-welcome (2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Empty metapackage for now — declares the runtime
    dependencies (PyGObject + GTK 4 + libadwaita + polkit) for the
    first-boot wizard. The Python source and policy file land in step 4
    of the v2.1-slim plan.

